{
    "background_story": "Ricardo was a shrewd businessman who built his fortune in the small town of Willow Creek. He started by buying out several local farms, eventually becoming the sole buyer of agricultural products in the area. As the town's only major employer, Ricardo's company, Green Earth Inc., had a stranglehold on the local labor market. Farmers and laborers had no choice but to sell their produce and services to Ricardo at the prices he dictated. His monopsony power allowed him to keep wages low and profits high. While some accused Ricardo of exploiting the townspeople, he argued that he was simply a savvy entrepreneur who had created a efficient and streamlined market. Love him or hate him, Ricardo's influence on Willow Creek was undeniable, and his name became synonymous with the town's economy.",
